node_modules
.next
out
.env*
# The template carries no secrets and is the only record of which variables
# the app needs, so it has to survive the blanket .env* rule above.
!.env.example
.DS_Store
.agents
skills-lock.json

# Build artifacts. `next-env.d.ts` is regenerated by `next dev` and
# `next build`, and Next rewrites its routes reference between the dev and
# production type paths — tracking it leaves the working tree permanently
# dirty. CI must therefore run `next build` (which regenerates it along with
# .next/types) rather than a bare `tsc --noEmit` on a clean checkout.
next-env.d.ts
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
*.log